  prose(<<~'CANONICAL_PROSE', origin: :published)
    ## Physical Character
    
    A geothermal vent in the western tunnels of Nightfall Shelf, rising from a chasm carved by its own heat. The vent releases mineral-heavy steam from depths that predate any penguin habitation — the ice-memory substrate here is among the oldest I have personally examined, and some of the impressions it holds are not penguin in origin. The locals call it the Bleeding Mouth. The name is earned.
    
    ## Early Settlement and Construction
    
    The Nightshelf built at the site during the Great Thaw, when geothermal access was survival rather than commerce. Carved channels and brazier-mounts remain visible beneath three distinct layers of repair, each executed in materials from a different era and guild — a stratigraphy of failed stabilization attempts. The most recent patching, in salvaged leather and mineral paste, followed the Abyss Collapse Tide, which split the thermal seams open. Master ice-carvers once decorated the forges here, artisans capable of reading ice-grain before the first pick struck. Their work carried names through the deeper tunnels. What survives of it is difficult to distinguish from the corruption damage.
    
    ## Corruption
    
    The corruption arrived in phases. The initial spread was slow — a creeping discoloration in the ice that could be mistaken for natural frost patterning by an untrained observer. The acceleration came after the discovery of ☽'moth Silvesiris~, a nearby corruption source-point, which saturated the cavern until Veil-render Seciae~, a Nightshelf purifier, burned it out. The char-marks Seciae~ left on the stone are still present. The ice-memory substrate suffered further degradation when the ☽'visois' Mask — an artifact that selects its own wielders through prolonged candidate evaluation — used the site's chambers for deep assessment across multiple selection cycles. The Mask's accumulated evaluation data left the substrate carrying more stored memory than its structure could support. During the geothermal catastrophe known as the Profun∴lapsum, dozens of candidates died, and the surrounding colony was driven into debt.
    
    The corruption at Thrall☽ Vavmastius is not resolved. It is managed, in the way that all corruption on The Berg is managed — incompletely.
    
    ## Midnight Claws Tenure
    
    The Midnight Claws, the syndicate that controlled Nightfall Shelf's shadow economy, seized the site after their herald Nanaiamis~ Praefectus brokered an agreement with the ☽'ofund' Guild, a Nightshelf trade faction. The Claws converted the space to ritual use: a shrine to The Way∴al, their doctrinal creed, and to Pactum∴myster, the blood-oath silence binding their Communion affiliates. Researchers continued working in sealed lower chambers, pursuing something designated Star∴eternal — a resonance phenomenon whose nature the available sources do not clarify.
    
    Nightshelf scripture attributes the Claws' ritual practices to the Order of the First Dark, their claimed predecessors, who reportedly fed bodies to the vents as sacred obligation and recorded the acts in ink on hide rather than in aurora ice-memory. Whether this lineage is genuine or retrospective legitimation, I cannot determine from the available record.
    
    The Shadow Parliament, Nightfall Shelf's wartime governing body, dissolved the Midnight Claws under Iudicium∴culum and declared all territorial claims forfeit. An unintended consequence: the Claws' rituals had maintained the ice-memory conduits the Mask depended on for evaluation. Without tending, the brazier-mounts went cold and the conduits silted with interference.
    
    ## Current Status
    
    Governance of Thrall☽ Vavmastius remains unresolved. The Collective☽ Of Led∴merch, a Nightshelf merchant guild, endorses the corridor through the chasm as the sole guild-escorted passage for moving deep-seam relics, with Void-Merchants operating as passage coordinators and providing tripartite fire-core certification at the junction. The Shadow Parliament maintains a rotating hall in the upper chambers for Night-Assessor business during after-tide hours. Magister ☽'Naevaeum~ Depth-walker, a Nightshelf hermit, serves as the site's guardian, tending the thermal vents and refusing visitors — though the Aurora Stack has learned to leave offerings at the approach, noting that something at the site deters orca incursion into the deeper tunnels.
    
    No single authority controls the Bleeding Mouth. Several occupy portions of it. The distinction matters.
  CANONICAL_PROSE
  annotation "note_1771577010962_0", anchor: "the Claws' rituals had maintained the ice-memory conduits the Mask depended on for evaluation", text: "How extraordinary that no one checked. The Shadow Parliament filed a dissolution under procedural law and accidentally severed the maintenance chain for an artifact older than penguin civilization. The conduit failure registers in the substrate as a cascading silence — channels darkening one by one over roughly nine tidal cycles. Someone in the Parliament must have noticed the Mask's assessment chamber going cold. The record does not show that anyone acted. A criminal syndicate had been performing the work of temple acolytes, and the governing body that dissolved them did not think to ask what the rituals were actually for.", type: :commentary, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771577010962_1", anchor: "a resonance phenomenon whose nature the available sources do not clarify", text: "They do not clarify because nothing in the sealed chambers clarifies. Star∴eternal appears in Claws inventories as a line item — no description, no methodology, no findings. Only requisition orders for fire-cores in quantities sufficient to heat a small colony, drawn over at least six tidal cycles. Whatever was being pursued consumed resources on a scale suggesting either genuine discovery or spectacular fraud, and the dissolution under Iudicium∴culum made no provision for continuing or even cataloguing the research. The chambers remain sealed. I requested access. The request remains unanswered. This is noted without expectation.", type: :skepticism, display: :full
  annotation "note_1771577010962_2", anchor: "Whether this lineage is genuine or retrospective legitimation", text: "Every syndicate that survives two generations discovers ancient predecessors. The Claws' claim follows the pattern precisely: sacred violence, solemn obligation, records kept on perishable media that cannot be verified at geothermal proximity over the timescales implied. Ink on hide does not survive the Bleeding Mouth.", type: :skepticism, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771577010962_3", anchor: "dozens of candidates died", text: "\"Dozens\" appears in three separate Nightshelf administrative filings that agree on nothing else about the Profun∴lapsum. The debt records — which have no reason to undercount, since larger losses justified larger claims — suggest approximately forty. I let \"dozens\" stand because the entry cannot carry the full accounting. But the number is not vague because the count was imprecise. It is vague because the bodies were not all recovered.", type: :correction, display: :popout
  annotation "note_1771577010962_4", anchor: "three distinct layers of repair, each executed in materials from a different era and guild", text: "Volcanicite and coral-paste (Great Thaw era, likely Fire Keeper guild-mark). Compressed aurora-ice bonded with krill adhesive (Faction Wars, unattributed — possibly military engineers). Salvaged leather and mineral paste (post-Abyss Collapse Tide, ☽'ofund' Guild stamp visible on two panels). Three eras of penguin engineering, each confident it had solved the problem. The vent split all three open along the same fault line.", type: :pedantic, display: :popout
